---
/**
 * Page-specific callout for docs/vault-layout.mdx: the one rule of filing,
 * lifted out of thin trailing prose into a single highlighted surface, plus a
 * two-pane demo that shows the failure and the fix side by side: the note
 * that waves at the source file versus the note that carries the rows. The
 * mock prices are schematic scaffolding, not product facts. Borderless filled
 * surfaces throughout (no border, no left bar). Scoped CSS, theme-aware via
 * Starlight --sl tokens with a light-theme override for the failure hue, root
 * carries `not-content` to keep Starlight's markdown margins out.
 */
---

<div class="rule not-content">
  <span class="label">the one rule of filing</span>
  <p class="line">
    Filing <strong>adds</strong>, it never removes.
  </p>
  <p class="sub">
    <code>recall</code> searches <code>vault/</code> only, so anything left behind in
    <code>raw/</code> (the folder of untouched originals) is invisible to it. The note has to
    carry the source's real <strong>payload</strong> in full: tables, lists, IDs, numbers,
    dates, prices, doses, exact wording. The summary goes on top of that, never in place of it.
  </p>

  <div class="demo">
    <section class="pane bad">
      <span class="ptag">the note that loses it</span>
      <div class="mock">
        <span class="mtitle"># health insurance</span>
        <p class="mline">Premiums went up this year.</p>
        <p class="mline gone">full table: see the source file</p>
      </div>
      <p class="verdict">The numbers stayed behind in <code>raw/</code>, where search never looks.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="pane good">
      <span class="ptag">the note that keeps it</span>
      <div class="mock">
        <span class="mtitle"># health insurance</span>
        <p class="mline">Premiums went up this year.</p>
        <table class="mtable">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>basic</td><td>89 &rarr; 104 /mo</td></tr>
            <tr><td>plus</td><td>129 &rarr; 151 /mo</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="verdict">The rows ride in the note, so any question about them has an answer.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="test">
    The test before a note is done: could you answer a specific question from the vault
    note alone, without opening the original? If the answer is only in <code>raw/</code>,
    you dropped the knowledge. Put it back.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .rule {
    --bad: #e09a86;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 1rem;
    padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 13%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  :global([data-theme="light"]) .rule {
    --bad: #a84a2e;
  }
  .label {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .line {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .line strong {
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .sub {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  .test {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }
  /* match the headline's accent emphasis so the callout reads one bold rank */
  .sub strong {
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .sub code,
  .test code,
  .verdict code {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    padding: 0.08rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-bg) 78%, var(--sl-color-text-accent));
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 22%, transparent);
  }

  /* ---- the two-pane demo ---- */
  .demo {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .pane {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }
  .pane.bad {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bad) 11%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .pane.good {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 15%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .ptag {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .pane.bad .ptag {
    color: var(--bad);
  }
  .pane.good .ptag {
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
  }
  .mock {
    padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-bg) 62%, transparent);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .mtitle {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }
  .mline {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }
  .mline.gone {
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
    color: var(--bad);
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .mtable {
    width: auto;
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
  }
  .mtable td {
    padding: 0.14rem 1.1rem 0.14rem 0;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-gray-3) 40%, transparent);
  }
  .mtable tr:first-child td {
    border-top: 0;
  }
  .mtable td:last-child {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    padding-right: 0;
  }
  .verdict {
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .line {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
    .demo {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
